# BlockML Libraries & Versioning

## Mandatory BML namespace

Every BML definition must reside under the owning domain's `bml` package:

```text
<domain>.bml.*     e.g. org.blockml.bml.* · com.machineblocks.bml.*
```

No Block, Library, Type, Language, Service, Capability, or other BlockML definition may exist outside `<domain>.bml.*`. Physical paths mirror FQNs: `blocks/org/blockml/bml/core/Block.bml` → `org.blockml.bml.core.Block`.

## Library structure

- Abstract base type: `org.blockml.bml.core.BlockLibrary` in `node_modules/@blockml/core/blocks/org/blockml/bml/core/BlockLibrary.bml`
- Framework base type — **not** exported via any Library `blocks`
- Concrete libraries: `<name>Library</name>`, filename **`Library.bml`**, `baseType="bcore:BlockLibrary"`
- FQN = `{package}.Library` from the file's package path
- **Membership is defined only by `Library.bml` `blocks`** — not by directories
- Catalog members (`description`, `language`, `readFirst`, `bootstrap`, `dependencies`, `subLibraries`, `schemas`, `blocks`) are **public** and **`readOnly`** — inspectable from foreign Blocks; authored only on the Library definition

## Nested libraries

Multiple `Library.bml` files may exist at different package levels (e.g. `org.blockml.bml.Library` + `org.blockml.bml.compiler.Library`).

```text
Typical:  inner dependencies → outer Library
Forbidden: outer blocks → Block exported by inner Library
Error:    BML_LIBRARY_NESTING_VIOLATION
```

## Effective block version

```text
effectiveBlockVersion =
  own <version>       if present
  else library.version if exported via Library blocks
  else error → BML_MISSING_VERSION
```

- **Framework blocks** (`org.blockml.bml.*`, `com.machineblocks.bml.*`): version only on `Library.bml`
- **Block in library** with own `<version>`: must be `>= library.version`
- **Standalone block**: `<version>` mandatory

## Instance references (`bml:version`)

- **Optional** on external references and Library TypeReferenceEntity sugar (`dependencies`,
  `subLibraries`, `blocks`, `readFirst`, `bootstrap`, `language`) — omitted = resolve from
  TypeRegistry / library context
- **Present** = exact-version assert against the **referenced** type (`value` for sugar) →
  `BML_UNKNOWN_VERSION` if no match
- Example dependency pin: `<blockml:Library bml:version="3.0.0" />`

## Library file pattern

```xml
<name>Library</name>
<baseType>bcore:BlockLibrary</baseType>
<version>3.0.0</version>
<dependencies>
  <composition><blockml:Library bml:version="3.0.0" /></composition>
</dependencies>
<blocks>
  <composition><bcore:Block /></composition>   <!-- export blocks, NOT BlockLibrary -->
</blocks>
```
